;
; How Binnacle files its waypoint tree in MYRA (binnacle_rules.h BR7):
; under the route (its place in the list of routes), the waypoint (its
; place on the route), then the waypoint's latitude and longitude in
; millionths of a degree. Binnacle asks whether the numbers fit before it
; keeps a waypoint on a route.
^ZXBINNACLE(route:i3, wpt:i3) = lat:i8! ^ lon:i9!
